PLUMED is an open-source, community-developed library that provides
a wide range of different methods, which include:
  - enhanced-sampling algorithms
  - free-energy methods
  - tools to analyze the vast amounts of data produced by molecular
  dynamics (MD) simulations.

These techniques can be used in combination with a large toolbox
of collective variables that describe complex processes in physics,
chemistry, material science, and biology.

PLUMED is an optional dependency of lammps. It is strictly required to
enable the module PLUMED in the build of lammps.

PLUMED can be compiled in serial or in parallel mode. The mode is
managed by the script as following:

By default, the script detects if a MPI package is installed in the
system. This can be alternatively:
- MPICH: installed with the package mpich
- OPEN MPI: installed with the package openmpi (not supported in 32-bit
            systems) or openmpi.
If a MPI package is installed, PLUMED will be build in parallel mode
using this. You can disable this option passing
    # MPI=no ./PLUMED.SlackBuild
    
If any MPI package is detected or you are disabled it with MPI=no, the
script enable the parallel mode using OpenMP available in a full
installation of Slackware. You can disable this option passing
    # MP=no ./PLUMED.SlackBuild 

The parallel mode with MPI will disable by default the support to
OpenMP. This can be by-passed setting the environment variable
    # MP=yes ./PLUMED.SlackBuild
In this case, the parallelization use bot MPI and MP    
    
If the support to MPI and openmp are both disabled, PLUMED will be
build in serial mode. To sum up:
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Context      | Environment variables | Mode
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
               | nothing (default)     | Parallel with MPI     
               -------------------------------------------------------- 
 MPICH or      | MPI=no                | Parallel with OpenMP 
 Open MPI      --------------------------------------------------------
 installed     | MP=yes                | Parallel with both OpenMP+MPI
               --------------------------------------------------------
               | MPI=no MP=no          | Serial
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
 Neither MPICH | nothing (default)     | Parallel with OpenMP
 nor Open MPI  --------------------------------------------------------
 installed     | MP=no                 | Serial
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Support to Python is enabled by default if python3-numpy and pybind11
are installed. Without one of these dependencies, the support to Python
will be disabled.
You can disable it in any case passing
    # PYTHON=no ./PLUMED.SlackBuild 
With the lastest condition, python3-numpy and pybind11 are not required.

PLUMED can use bundle libraries for linear algebra, but his performance
takes advantage using external optimized blas/lapack libraries, so 
OpenBLAS is required as dependency. Since it could conflict with OpenMP
when used in parallelization, it would be better to disable support to
OpenMP and build PLUMED against a MPI package.

The documentation is available at 
https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-doc/html/index.html
